{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"One last source-only sharpening of the removed-member refutation rather than a new finding. In the same select loop that carries the removed-node proposal block, the receive-channel case filters response messages from peers that are not in Progress while the proposal-channel case applies no membership test, and the removed-node block that nils the proposal channel is the local convenience whose own comment calls the logic unsound and notes the channel is reset on a leader change. Recording that deliberate asymmetry strengthens the refutation, which now rests on two independent bases: the documented MsgProp contract, under which a leader appends what it receives and a follower forwards with the sender's ID, and the fact that the library does consult membership for responses but not for proposals. No defect is asserted, no execution is claimed, and the earlier behaviour facts are unchanged, including that a proposal whose sender is not in the configuration is accepted and appended at the raft level. The addendum's limitations state that the asymmetry is evidence about intent rather than a normative requirement, and that a reader could still argue the leader ought to check membership, which would be a design change rather than a defect under the current contract. The rest of the run stands as recorded: two asserted defects with retained executions, namely read-index retry growth with its measured retention, burst, CheckQuorum control, byte measurement and network-exercised amplification, and the accepted-then-panicking empty non-Auto configuration change with its end-to-end commit demonstration and Auto control.\"}"}}
